@page rh="CHRONICLES · 5 OF 6 · THE SANCTIONED RETELLING · WRITING" m="WRITING; 2 CHR 36; TKC: DOM · TL"
# Write the Empire's second telling
Dominion has an official history of the Fall. Chronicles shows how a sanctioned retelling actually behaves. It keeps more than you expect, adds liturgy, moves blame without deleting the event, and ends on the note it wants remembered. Build yours on that model and not on crude deletion.
prompt: 1 · What the Empire's history of the Fall keeps, even though it's damaging | fill
prompt: 2 · Where it moves the blame without removing the event | fill
prompt: 3 · The liturgy it adds. What the official version has that the old one didn't | fill
prompt: 4 · The last sentence of the official history, drafted word for word | fill

